From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dmitry Afonchenko <undermove1@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 13:49:50 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] Meridian: the Boost badge's glints and the tiles' hover, our
 own motion on Arc's principles
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The owner: "similar, not the same". From the motion measured on Arc
(S/arc-px/MOTION.md) we keep the principles: a calm loop on its own, each
spark ~0.85 s growing and fading as sin(pi t) with no opacity fade, at most
three, staggered, a rest before the next round, still icons on hover. Ours:
- a six-ray glint with a round core (not a four-point star), drifting 40°
  anticlockwise on a ring round the brush (not turning in place), warming
  from cream to the boost's own pale colour at its peak; a 2 s round,
  starts 0 / 0.32 / 0.62 s, a 0.6 s rest;
- the tiles darken by the same step but ease in over 70 ms.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SwxrQ2eLfJ2bv8cCoG2va1
